    <article><h3>Hot weather</h3><p>Heat and sweating increase water loss.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Long or hard activity</h3><p>Exercise can make fluid and electrolyte planning more relevant.</p><a href="/pages/active-living">Active Living →</a></article>
    <article><h3>Travel</h3><p>Access and routine can be disrupted by flights, road trips and long days.</p><a href="/pages/travel-hydration">Travel →</a></article>
    <article><h3>Illness or medical conditions</h3><p>Some conditions require more fluid, while others require restriction. Follow clinical guidance when appropriate.</p><a href="/pages/clinical-hydration">Clinical Hydration →</a></article>
  </div>
</section>

